{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WedderburnWeightCanonical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WedderburnWeightCanonical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta_mul_h_eq_neg_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta_mul_h_eq_neg_C","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L141-L153","doc":"**Cross-ratio, division-free form**: `β · h = -C` for every `λ`.\n\nThis is the multiplicative relation behind `β / C = -1/h`: in a\nfield, dividing by `C ≠ 0` and `h ≠ 0` recovers the ratio form, and\nconversely.  Stated multiplicatively it needs *no* nonvanishing\nhypotheses at all — both sides are `-½ · w_λ · h` — so it holds in\nthe coefficient ring where the weights actually live. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.C_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.C_eq","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L139-L139","doc":"LP shadow-price scaling identity (all λ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta_eq","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L137-L137","doc":"BW scaling identity (all λ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.y","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Markov coefficient `y_λ(q)` (Wenzl closed form; abstract\nhere, supplied per instance).  Data only — no axiom relates it\nto `w`; see the module docstring for the dropped identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.C","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L131-L131","doc":"LP shadow-price `C_λ = tilde w_λ · h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.beta","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L129-L129","doc":"BW mass coefficient `β_λ = -½ tilde w_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.kappa","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L127-L127","doc":"Content sum `κ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.w","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The canonical q-deformed Wedderburn weight `tilde w_λ ∈ R`\n(Laurent in `q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.h","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The Hecke-generator scalar `h = q - q⁻¹` in `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnWeightCanonical","kind":"class","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L106-L139","doc":"The canonical Wedderburn-block weight discipline, polymorphic in\nthe ground ring `R`.\n\nAn instance asserts:\n  • the BW mass coefficient `β_λ = -½ tilde w_λ` (for all λ);\n  • the LP shadow-price `C_λ = tilde w_λ · h/2` (for all λ).\n\nIt carries the Markov coefficient `y_λ` (Wenzl's hook–content closed\nform [wenzl1988]) as **data only**.  The self-conjugate Wenzl-bridge\nidentity `y_λ = tilde w_λ` on `κ_λ = 0` was a field here until\n2026-09-04; it is false at the intended values (module docstring) and\nwas dropped on the owner's ruling.  No relation between `y` and `w`\nis asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","kind":"structure","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-weight-canonical.lean#L99-L103","doc":"A partition (placeholder; the canonical weight is parameterised\nover an abstract partition type so the discipline holds for any\nrealisation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}